 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34CL2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34CL dE EAV,LOGFT$From BetaShape v2.4 (Jun-2024) 2023Mo21.                     
 34CL dG CC$FROM BrIcc v2.3e (17-Jun-2020) 2008Ki07, "Frozen Orbitals" appr.    
 34CL dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 12-Jun-2026)          
 34CL c  2020Ia01: a 30-MeV/nucleon {+35}Cl beam was produced from the K500     
 34CL2c  cyclotron at Texas A&M University and impinged on a                    
 34CL3c  liquid-nitrogen-cooled hydrogen gas target. The fully stripped reaction
 34CL4c  products recoiled into the Momentum Achromat Recoil Spectrometer       
 34CL5c  (MARS), where they were spatially separated according to their         
 34CL6c  charge-to-mass ratio. A 99.5% pure {+34}Ar beam was implanted into     
 34CL7c  aluminized Mylar tape of a fast tape-transport system and then moved to
 34CL8c  a well-shielded location 90 cm away. Decay positrons were detected     
 34CL9c  using a 4|p proportional gas counter. Nearly 12000 collect-move-detect 
 34CLAc  cycles were repeated and a total of 1.7|*10{+8} decay positrons were   
 34CLBc  recorded. Measured E|b, |b(t). Deduced T{-1/2} of {+34}Ar.             
 34CL c  2020Ia02: similar setup as 2020Ia01. Nearly 70000 collect-move-detect  
 34CL2c  cycles were repeated. A total of 2.6710|*10{+8} {I20} decay positrons  
 34CL3c  were recorded. Decay positrons were detected using a 1-mm-thick BC-404 
 34CL4c  scintillator and |g rays were detected using a HPGe detector. Measured 
 34CL5c  E|b, E|g, |b|g-coin. Deduced levels, decay branching ratios, log {Ift},
 34CL6c  Gamow-Teller strengths. Comparisons with shell-model calculations.     
 34CL c  2006Ia05: similar setup as 2020Ia01. Measured T{-1/2} of {+34}Ar.      
 34CL c  1974Ha26: {+34}Ar was produced via the {+32}S({+3}He,n) reaction with a
 34CL2c  12-MeV {+3}He beam from the Chalk River MP tandem accelerator, fast    
 34CL3c  gas-transport system, Ge(Li) detector. Measured I|g, E|g, T{-1/2}, and 
 34CL4c  absolute |e+|b{++} branching ratios.                                   
 34CL c  Others: 1972Ha58 (T{-1/2}), 1971Mo27 (I|g, E|g, T{-1/2}).              
 34CL c  The decay scheme is considered fairly complete. Shell-model            
 34CL2c  calculations estimate the possible unobserved |b-feeding intensities to
 34CL3c  higher excited states in {+34}Cl to be <0.005%, more than an           
 34CL4c  order-of-magnitude less than the quoted uncertainty (2020Ia02).        
 34CL cE TI$Deduced from |g-ray intensity balance, relative to I|g(666)=100,    
 34CL2cE normalized to absolute %I|g(666|g)=0.0248 {I28}, which was dedcued from
 34CL3cE the measured counts of |g rays and positrons.                          
 34CL cG E$No E|g with uncertainty is given by any paper in this dataset. If a  
 34CL2cG |g transition is to the g.s. and also the strongest |g branch, the E|g 
 34CL3cG is deduced from the level energy. Other E|g values are deduced from the
 34CL4cG level energy differences.                                              
 34CL cG RI$I|g are from 2020Ia02, which takes into account their own data,     
 34CL2cG 1974Ha26, 1990En08, and an unpublished (p,|g) I|g data by one of the   
 34CL3cG authors of 2020Ia02.                                                   
 34CL cG M,MR$From the Adopted Gammas.                                          
 34CL cL E$Level energies with uncertainties are from 1974Ha26 based on measured
 34CL2cL E|g. Level energies without uncertainties are rounded from the Adopted 
 34CL3cL Levels.                                                                
